      },
      "message": "feat(sim): plasma through-cut laws - cut order, kerf crossing, tip-up\n\n#672 step 1 (part of #621's plasma research): sim::verify::plasma judges\na plasma program from a neutral form - the kerf, the cuts in order (each\nthe torch-on polyline with its contour id, inner/outer and parent outer)\nand the rapid into each - so it reads the CL's torch records (#670) and\nnothing of the operation's internals:\n- cut order (refusal): an inner contour cut after the outer that frees\n  its part;\n- kerf crossing (warning): a cut within one kerf of an earlier cut's\n  centre line - the THC dive the LinuxCNC Plasma Primer §12 warns of;\n- tip-up (warning): a rapid across a part already cut free (Tormach\n  1300PL manual UM10720 §1.4.2, §4.12.8);\n- malformed (refusal): a non-positive or non-finite kerf, a NaN point, a\n  cut with no path.\nNot yet wired: step 2 reads the plasma op's CL torch records (#670) and\nblocks the post on a refusal.\n\nPinned by plasma_laws (5): each law tripped by one fixture and passed by\nanother.\n\nRefs #672\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
