      "message": "fix(sim): plasma laws judge any enclosing contour, roles, and refuse what they can't judge\n\nReview of #675:\n- Cut order is judged against ANY enclosing contour (the parent chain #670\n  writes): an island cut after its hole is refused, as a hole after its\n  outline was. CutOrder { contour, enclosing }.\n- Contours carry a role (Outer / Inner / Open, matching the CL's TORCH ON\n  C<id> OUTER|INNER|OPEN) and a small-hole flag; an open path is never a\n  freed area for tip-up; a centre-pierced small hole may be one point.\n- Refused by name as Malformed: a duplicate contour id, a parent that is\n  the contour itself or no cut carries, an inner contour with no parent,\n  a rapid list that does not match the cuts, a NaN rapid point.\n- The module doc says kerf crossing covers only the torch-height hazard\n  (a warning; shared-kerf common lines are legal) and a true crossing\n  becomes a refusal with the CL reader in step 2. mod order fixed.\n\nPinned by plasma_laws (8): an_island_after_its_hole_is_refused,\nbad_parents_ids_and_rapids_are_refused_by_name,\nsmall_holes_and_open_paths, plus the five step-1 laws.\n\nRefs #672\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
